## Verdicts

| Verdict | When |
|---|---|
| `{{approved_word}}` | All criteria in `SKILL.md` met on the review revision |
| `{{changes_word}}` | Any blocking finding (incl. CONFIRMED bug-hunt BLOCKER/MAJOR, failing gate or test) |
| `{{blocked_word}}` | Required evidence missing (gate cannot run, PLAUSIBLE BLOCKER unresolved) — name the evidence |

`NOT_RUN` and `BLOCKED` checks are never `PASS`.

## No waivers

The reviewer cannot excuse a rule violation. A real conflict with the approved design goes back to {{planning_gate}} / the user, as `{{changes_word}}` or `{{blocked_word}}`.

## Rounds

- After a fix: review the **new** revision — the fix diff, the findings it claims to close, and rerun the checks it affects.
- Disputes: {{objection_path}}.
- The same finding returned a third time → escalate to {{escalation_role}} with both positions.

